+ a material consisting of many of them, as *hair*, *straw*; (E) Nouns denoting either a material or a collection of things made of it, as *linen*, *silver*, *china*;
>>>

<<<
(F) Nouns denoting either a thing or some or all of them, as fruit, timber; (G) Abstract singulars used instead of concrete plurals, as accommodation (=rooms), kindling (=pieces of wood), royalty (= royal persons), pottery (=pots);
===
(F) Nouns denoting either a thing or some or all of them, as *fruit*, *timber*; (G) Abstract singulars used instead of concrete plurals, as *accommodation* (=rooms), *kindling* (=pieces of wood), *royalty* (=royal persons), *pottery* (=pots);
>>>

